Part of my previous forum comment about this topic:

The term "Anime" is a different meaning for westeners and japanese people. Anime for westerners is everything that is inheritently made and produced in Japan (Sound composition or help from smaller studios don't count). On the other hand the term Anime means for japanese people everything that is 2D and 3D animated since it's a japanese word for them and our term Anime is a word that we took over but changed the meaning of. Therefore, Avatar the last airbender is NOT an anime since it was purely produced in the US. Of course it contains elements in it that are derived from anime but in the first place it is a cartoon. That is also the reason why we do not call donghua "Anime". Even though it has the exact same artstyle it was produced in China and honestly, as a chinese person I would also be pissed if someone called donghua "Anime" since in that case people would automatically connect the show to Japan.

